course: dictionary
lesson: 4156
title: Time zones and GMT
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every place on Earth has its own time, because the Sun rises at different times in different places. To keep the world organised, clocks start from one agreed point: GMT, Greenwich Mean Time. Greenwich is in London, and it is the zero point for time zones.
explain: Time zones work like steps around the world. Places to the east of Greenwich are ahead of GMT, and places to the west are behind. «New York is 5 hours behind London» tells you New York is to the west, so its clock shows an earlier time.
explain: «Tokyo is 9 hours ahead» means Tokyo is to the east, so when it is noon in London, it is already 9 pm in Tokyo. «India is 5 and a half hours ahead» shows that time zones can be half-hours apart, not only whole hours.
explain: Be careful with summer. In winter the UK uses GMT, but in summer it uses British Summer Time, one hour ahead of GMT. Writing «GMT+1» means one hour ahead of GMT, and «GMT-5» means five hours behind it.
fact: GMT stands for Greenwich Mean Time.
fact: Greenwich is in London, and it is the starting point for the world's time zones.
fact: «GMT+1» means one hour ahead of GMT; «GMT-5» means five hours behind GMT.
fact: In winter the UK uses GMT, which is equal to UTC.
fact: In summer the UK uses British Summer Time, one hour ahead of GMT.
exercise: In winter, which time does the UK use? | *GMT | Beijing time | New York time | British Summer Time, one hour ahead of GMT
exercise: «New York is 5 hours behind London.» Is New York to the east or the west of Greenwich? | South | *West | North | East
exercise: «Tokyo is 9 hours ahead of London.» What does this tell you about Tokyo's clock? | It shows exactly the same time as London | It has stopped | *It shows a later time than London | It shows an earlier time than London
test: What does GMT stand for? | *Greenwich Mean Time | Global Mean Time | Great Midday Time | Ground Mean Table
test: «Beijing is 8 hours ahead of London.» If it is 3 pm in London, what time is it in Beijing? | 5 pm | 7 am | *11 pm | 3 pm
exam: In summer, British Summer Time is how many hours ahead of GMT? | *One hour | Two hours | Half an hour | Zero hours
